Z||000000||jlhuber||10-12-1999||08:51 PM||||i have an '86 gt with the auto tranny.  when the engine is cold it runs good oil pressure (70-80psi), but when it heats up it runs so low it scares me to drive it anywhere (10-0psi).  do i have a faulty oil pressure gauge, or is there a problem with the internals of the engine?  it has been suggested that my oil pump could be bad or i could have spun a cam bearing.  this motor has been rebuilt once from a spun cam bearing resulting in siezure.  also, when it is at operating temperature and i stop at stoplight for a long time or numerous ones, it wants to overheat and quit.  is that just caused by the netorious fiero cooling prob?needless to say, i'm stumpped.  any help would be great.||||reg||5
Z||000001||mwbackus||10-12-1999||09:13 PM||||If your oil pressure is acutually that low when its full to the mark, it would very likely shut down the fuel pump.  This could be the exact cause of your stoplight problems.  Replace the sender, and if that does not immediatly fix things, I would park it and inspect things more thoughly. It could be something as simple as the oil pump tube falling off the pump, so caution would be the best policy.<P>Mike<p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 10-12-1999).]||||reg||1
